   "id": "5d51c167",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Row deletion eliminates almost every record here because nearly every row has at least one missing field. Column deletion removes any column with even one null. In practice, targeted deletion — dropping only columns or rows above a missingness threshold — is more useful.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Imputation** replaces missing values with plausible substitutes. The `fillna` method covers the most common strategies:"
   ]
