   "source": [
    "## Inconsistent Data Types\n",
    "\n",
    "Pandas infers column types when loading a file, but inference is not always correct. Wrong types break operations silently — averaging a column of numbers stored as strings produces an error, and comparing dates stored as text gives alphabetical rather than chronological ordering. The goal is for every column to have a type that matches its meaning.\n",
    "\n",
    "Useful inspection tools: `dtypes`, `info()`, `head()`, and `unique()`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 19,
   "id": "0fd89748",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "date        str\n",
      "price       str\n",
      "in_stock    str\n",
      "dtype: object\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "example_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"date\":    [\"2024-01-01\", \"2024-01-02\", \"2024-01-03\"],\n",
    "    \"price\":   [\"1.10\", \"2.20\", \"3.30\"],\n",
    "    \"in_stock\": [\"True\", \"False\", \"True\"],\n",
    "})\n",
    "print(example_df.dtypes)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "466606a6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "All three columns are read as `object` (string). Each needs to be coerced to its correct type.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Dates stored as strings"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 20,
   "id": "ce8f4f29",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Before: str\n",
      "After:  datetime64[us]\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "print(f\"Before: {example_df['date'].dtype}\")\n",
    "example_df['date'] = pd.to_datetime(example_df['date'])\n",
    "print(f\"After:  {example_df['date'].dtype}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "bf694062",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Numbers stored as strings"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 21,
   "id": "3e741d4c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Before: str\n",
      "After:  float64\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "print(f\"Before: {example_df['price'].dtype}\")\n",
    "example_df['price'] = pd.to_numeric(example_df['price'])\n",
    "print(f\"After:  {example_df['price'].dtype}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a62856c3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Booleans stored as strings"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
